  <span class="mono-label">RING 1 · CORNERSTONE</span>
  <h1>What should I do this summer if I didn't get an internship?</h1>
  <p class="answer-capsule">Build receipts. Pick 3 to 5 tasks in your target role, complete them against deadlines, and submit for scoring. A summer of scored work is stronger signal than a blank resume line.</p>

  <div class="tldr">
    <ul>
      <li>Recruiters evaluate trajectory, not just credentials.</li>
      <li>A blank summer looks like waiting. A productive summer looks like creating.</li>
      <li>3 to 5 receipts in one function show commitment and growth.</li>
      <li>Most zero tasks take 3 to 7 days. You can build 8 in a summer.</li>
      <li>Optimize for output, not completion.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <section>
    <h2>Why does a blank summer hurt your hiring chances?</h2>
    <p>Recruiters evaluate trajectory. A student who did nothing over the summer looks like a student who waits for opportunities. A student who built four receipts looks like a student who creates them. The difference is not talent: it is signal.</p>
    <p>You do not need an internship to build signal. You need a task, a deadline, and a rubric. zero gives you all three.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What is the best use of a summer without an internship?</h2>
    <p>Pick one role direction. Complete 3 to 5 tasks in that direction. Submit each for scoring. Use the feedback to iterate. By the end of the summer, you have a portfolio range and a percentile trajectory that recruiters can evaluate in seconds.</p>
    <p>The key is consistency. One receipt is interesting. Three receipts in the same function show commitment and growth. Five receipts show you are serious.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How do I choose which tasks to do?</h2>
    <p>Start with the role you want. If you want product, do product tasks. If you want marketing, do marketing tasks. If you are unsure, do one task in each of three functions and see which one you finish fastest and best. That is your signal.</p>
    <p>See <a href="/how-it-works">how zero works</a> or browse <a href="/receipts">live receipts</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="author-bio">
    <p><strong>Atul Khola</strong> is Head of Experience at zero. He has led design and product at CRED, cult.fit, topper, and media.net. He lectures at IITs, NIDs, and NIFTs on product design and career strategy.</p>
  </section>

